# Whether a key gets a release follows from its press (ADR-1005 D7, the
# maintainer's decision of 2026-11-13). Under flag 2 alone, a key that makes
# text sends its text on a press, and its release as CSI 97 ; 1:3 u. A key
# pressed under flags 3, Ctrl+a, gets its release after the flags are popped
# to 0, with the code its press used and the modifiers at the release,
# Ctrl let go. A key pressed while flag 2 was not in force gets no release,
# even once a program pushes flag 2. A release with no press sends nothing.
# spec: kitty's Comprehensive keyboard handling in terminals: Report event types, Event types, Legacy key event encoding; ADR-1005 D7 and D13 slice 3
# covers: input.kitty-keyboard
size 20 2
send "\e[>2u"
cmd key;sym=61;ascii=61;unicode=61
cmd key;sym=61;ascii=61;unicode=61;event=release
send "\e[>3u"
cmd key;sym=61;ascii=61;unicode=61;mods=4
send "\e[<2u\e[?u"
cmd key;sym=61;ascii=61;unicode=61;event=release
cmd key;sym=61;ascii=61;unicode=61;mods=4
send "\e[>2u\e[?u"
cmd key;sym=61;ascii=61;unicode=61;event=release
cmd key;sym=ff52;event=release
